] [17592186434175 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434175 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186434159 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434175 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f41511bf-d7bf-5d58-801e-068f8384039f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434176 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434176 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434176 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434126 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434176 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434176 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434176 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434176 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434176 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186434102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434176 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f68303ba-d3f6-5ad1-af0c-d38e73240e24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434177 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434177 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60096" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434177 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434177 #edb/ref 1071 "The ratio of boys to the total number of children in a birthday party is $4:7.$ What is the meaning of this ratio?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434177 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "02447e62-a41a-5aec-b911-74025102ad42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434177 #edb/ref 1074 "If the ratio of boys to total children is $4:7,$ it means that there are $4$ boys for every $7$ children at the birthday party.\n\nAnother way of writing this is to say that \"out of every $7$ children at the birthday party, $4$ of them are boys.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434178 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434165 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434178 #edb/ref 1069 "q-70129" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434178 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434178 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/4f/4f6801c9bb82b4ba0a3ac2d16bf9d06799d0349ff718fbc31429cd74d054bcbe.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of triangles to hexagons?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434178 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0ff410a3-0c6f-5988-88a5-79160a3d1565" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434178 #edb/ref 1074 "We can express the ratio of the number of triangles to the number of hexagons as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of triangles}:\\text{number of hexagons}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of triangles. There are $2$ triangles.\n\n- Next, we count the number of hexagons. There are $3$ hexagons.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of triangles to hexagons is $2:3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434179 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434179 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60097" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434179 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434179 #edb/ref 1071 "The ratio of dogs to the total number of pets in a veterinary clinic is $2:5.$ What is the meaning of this ratio?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434179 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1f1c065d-26db-5359-ab36-7049627505ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434179 #edb/ref 1074 "If the ratio of dogs to total pets is $2:5,$ it means that there are $2$ dogs for every $5$ pets in the clinic.\n\nAnother way of writing this is to say that \"out of every $5$ pets in the clinic, $2$ of them are dogs.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434180 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434180 #edb/ref 1069 "q-70132" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434180 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434180 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ea/eab3931ef4d46de23144f52420557e790a7e041231fec22d6819891e8e92ab16.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of hexagons to pentagons?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434180 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "30f78782-46a8-5fef-93fa-62c3bc5d1001" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434180 #edb/ref 1074 "We can express the ratio of the number of hexagons to the number of pentagons as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of hexagons}:\\text{number of pentagons}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of hexagons. There are $2$ hexagons.\n\n- Next, we count the number of pentagons. There are $3$ pentagons.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of hexagons to pentagons is $2:3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434181 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434161 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434181 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434181 #edb/ref 1069 "q-235954" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434181 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434181 #edb/ref 1071 "Matt decides to distribute some candy to his best friends. The following table shows the number of candies each of his friends received. \n\n| Friends | Rose | Peter | Adriana | Vanessa | Helen | Luis | Jason |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Candies | $5$ | $6$ | $10$ | $9$ | $4$ | $3$ | $6$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWhat is the ratio of friends who received at least $8$ pieces of candy to those who received less than $8$ pieces of candy?\n\nThe required ratio is{{field-1}}\n$:$\n{{field-2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434181 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "342633b7-0af2-5736-9e7c-f7ff7859c8c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434181 #edb/ref 1074 "From the table, there are $2$ friends (Adriana and Vanessa) who received at least $8$ candies.\n\nOn the other hand, there are $5$ friends (Rose, Peter, Helen, Luis, and Jason) who received less than $8$ candies.\n\nSo the ratio of friends who received at least $8$ pieces of candy to those who received less than $8$ pieces of candy is $2:5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434182 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434166 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434182 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434182 #edb/ref 1069 "q-235814" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434182 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434182 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/38/38f113226c13332a07fdd6059819de5cf69147dbbfea3d1710325ef7776e5538.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the ratio of pentagons to the total number of shapes is{{field-1}}\n$:$\n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434182 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "348bf862-0000-5608-8f25-158f815d9723" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434182 #edb/ref 1074 "We can express the ratio of the number of pentagons to the total number of shapes as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of pentagons}:\\text{total number of shapes}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of pentagons. There are $4$ pentagons.\n\n- Next, we count the total number of shapes. There are $7$ shapes.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of pentagons to the total number of shapes is $4:7.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434183 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434183 #edb/ref 1069 "q-101428" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434183 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434183 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/7b/7b309bd6e44f1a1bc2e179dbcf50e6672366f69be364ae55b482cea16c680553.png)\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing numbers in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of hexagons to pentagons is $4:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there are $\\,\\boxed{}\\,$ hexagons for every $1$ pentagon." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434183 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "86a8860d-3cfb-576b-a5c9-f9833c8b5308" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434183 #edb/ref 1074 "We can express the ratio of the number of hexagons to the number of pentagons as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of hexagons}:\\text{number of pentagons}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of hexagons. There are $4$ hexagons.\n\n- Next, we count the number of pentagons. There is $1$ pentagon.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of hexagons to pentagons is $4:1.$\n\nSo, the missing numbers are  $1$ and $4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434184 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434184 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132025" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434184 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434184 #edb/ref 1071 "To make waffles, Joshua mixes $5$ eggs, $1$ cup of sugar, $200$ grams of butter, and $1$ cup of flour. What ratio describes the amount of sugar to the amount of flour?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434184 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "918c0ed9-8664-5aaa-af07-0b9b79fff05b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434184 #edb/ref 1074 "We can express the ratio of the amount of sugar to the amount of flour as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{amount of sugar}:\\text{amount of flour}\n$$\n\nWe compute our ratio as follows:\n\n- First, we count the amount of sugar. There is $1$ cup of sugar.\n\n- Next, we count the amount of flour. There is $1$ cup of flour.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of sugar to flour is $1:1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434185 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434185 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131916" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434185 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434185 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/b8/b8fb2d8be9596083481f83e6c8bacbb6a988ad527ef0a468583c239ea5e43838.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of triangles to the total number of shapes?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434185 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "94b6267e-404d-5206-b721-940a636b7569" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434185 #edb/ref 1074 "We can express the ratio of the number of triangles to the total number of shapes as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of triangles}:\\text{total number of shapes}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of triangles. There are $2$ triangles.\n\n- Next, we count the total number of shapes. There are $7$ shapes.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of triangles to total shapes is $2:7.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434186 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434186 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60094" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434186 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434186 #edb/ref 1071 "The table below represents the ages of players of a volleyball team. \n\n| Student | James | Robert | Charles | Daniel | Thomas | David |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Age (years) | $11$ | $9$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ | $10$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWhat is the ratio of players who are aged $10$ years or more to those who are less than $10$ years old?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434186 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a57c2b2f-5eb9-5b18-919a-0a3e3924e394" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434186 #edb/ref 1074 "From the table, there are $4$ players (James, Daniel, Thomas, David) whose age is $10$ or more years.\n\nThere are $2$ students (Robert, Charles)  whose age is less than $10$ years.\n\nSo the ratio of students whose age is $10$ or more years to those whose age is less than $10$ years is $4:2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434187 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434187 #edb/ref 1069 "q-59597" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434187 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434187 #edb/ref 1071 "The ratio of chocolate chip cookies to total cookies in a bakeshop is $8:10.$ What is the meaning of this ratio?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434187 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c0762ea5-0707-5974-8961-e278eb0de7ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434187 #edb/ref 1074 "If the ratio of chocolate chip cookies to total cookies is $8:10,$ it means that there are $8$ chocolate chip cookies for every $10$ cookies in total.\n\nAnother way of writing this is to say that \"out of every $10$ cookies in the shop, $8$ of them are chocolate chip.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434188 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434176 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434188 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131946" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434188 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434188 #edb/ref 1071 "To make a fruit sponge, Dimo mixes $3$ pounds of cherries with $2$ pounds of raisins. What ratio describes the amount of cherries to the amount of raisins?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434188 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e2300841-eb93-50ec-a81c-b69a7df78772" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434188 #edb/ref 1074 "We can express the ratio of the amount of cherry to the amount of raisins as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{amount of cherry}:\\text{amount of raisins}\n$$\n\nWe compute our ratio as follows:\n\n- First, we count the amount of cherries. There are $3$ pounds of cherries.\n\n- Next, we count the amount of raisins. There are $2$ pounds of raisins.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of cherries to raisins is $3:2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434189 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434160 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434189 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434163 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434189 #edb/ref 1069 "q-235951" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434189 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434189 #edb/ref 1071 "A study group contains $5$ freshmen, $4$ sophomores, and $3$ juniors. What ratio describes the number of freshmen to the total number of students?\n\nThe required ratio is{{field-1}}\n$:$\n{{field-2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434189 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e473c68b-cf42-5029-bb25-6a6af2c13e5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434189 #edb/ref 1074 "We can express the ratio of the number of freshmen to the total number of students as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of freshmen}:\\text{total number of students}\n$$\n\nWe compute our ratio as follows:\n\n- First, we count the number of freshmen. There are $5$ freshmen.\n\n- Next, we count the total number of students. There are $5+4+3=12$ students.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of freshmen to the total number of students is $5:12.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434190 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434190 #edb/ref 1069 "q-101429" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434190 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434190 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/38/382d511b0797e5b5800bfabc45ab83be7c57439cfe8a4e76da7cfce7f6888661.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of circles to pentagons?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434190 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa02dad0-56c6-5504-ac96-8894e78cb09f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434190 #edb/ref 1074 "We can express the ratio of the number of circles to the number of pentagons as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of circles}:\\text{number of pentagons}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of circles. There are $2$ circles.\n\n- Next, we count the number of pentagons. There are $2$ pentagons.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of circles to pentagons is $2:2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
